.TH LIBMPQ__PATCH_PAYLOAD_READ 3 2026-10-06 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__patch_payload_read \- read one decoded PTCH payload.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__patch_payload_read("
.BI "        mpq_archive_s *" "archive,"
.BI "        uint32_t " "file_number,"
.BI "        const char *" "filename,"
.BI "        uint8_t *" "buffer,"
.BI "        libmpq__off_t " "capacity,"
.BI "        libmpq__off_t *" "transferred"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Decode a member flagged \fBLIBMPQ_FILE_FLAG_PATCH_FILE\fP into caller-owned
\fIbuffer\fP. The returned bytes begin with PTCH, excluding the plaintext
patch-info prefix. The prefix's MD5 is checked against the decoded body.
\fIfilename\fP is the physical archive name for key derivation and may be
NULL if no name-derived key is needed. The function does not apply the patch
to a base file; BSD0 payloads require the matching base for materialization.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero and stores the byte count in \fItransferred\fP on success.
On failure, \fItransferred\fP is zero and a negative libmpq error is returned.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST
The archive, output pointer, file number, or patch-file flag is absent.
.TP
.B LIBMPQ_ERROR_SIZE
\fIcapacity\fP is too small, negative, or its nonempty buffer is NULL.
.TP
.B LIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT
The prefix, decoded size, or payload MD5 is invalid.
.PP
Allocation, I/O, decryption, and decompression errors may also propagate.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq__patch_payload_size (3),
.BR libmpq__file_read (3),
.BR libmpq__file_flags (3)
